The upstream Cargo.toml declares license = "MIT". Neither the published archive
nor the upstream repository inspected for this patch includes a separate LICENSE
or NOTICE file. LICENSE-MIT supplies the standard MIT terms corresponding to
that declaration; this notice does not invent an upstream copyright year.
All source comments and the original package metadata are retained.

The archive was checked against the root Cargo.lock checksum before copying.
The original Cargo.lock and Cargo cache marker were not copied. Original file
hashes are recorded in ../pdf-extract-upstream-files.json. This directory alone
contains local changes; the registry cache was not edited.

Local addition: opt-in, bounded marked-content ActualText extraction. The
original extraction APIs and the no-ActualText output path remain unchanged.
This is not a new PDF parser, a renderer, OCR, a reading-order solver, or a
sandbox for decompression and hostile PDF parsing.

The Type3 audit recognizes a strictly validated leading d0/d1 width declaration
because lopdf 0.42's content operator lexer does not accept digits. The complete
remaining glyph program is strict-parsed; remaining Type3 d operators are
conservatively unverified (including genuine dash-setting d). This helper does
not edit source bytes, render glyphs, or change legacy text extraction.
